Subject: [PATCH] H432B: reuse the selected Linux UBI attachment

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [H432B A/B boot contract]

Slot-state access already attaches this partition. Preserve that attachment
for the kernel read rather than tearing it down and rescanning all PEBs.
Explicit ubi part commands retain their original reattach semantics.

--- a/common/cmd_ubi.c
+++ b/common/cmd_ubi.c
@@ -1,1 +1,12 @@
-/* Dedicated dynamic environment copies, never a raw NAND offset. */
+int h432b_ubi_attach_linux(void)
+{
+	if (ubi_initialized && ubi && ubi_dev.selected &&
+	    !strcmp(ubi_dev.part_name, "linux"))
+		return 0;
+	if (run_command("mtdparts default", 0))
+		return -EINVAL;
+	return run_command("ubi part linux", 0);
+}
+
+
+/* Dedicated dynamic environment copies, never a raw NAND offset. */
